A||||4||rodmcneill||T tops vs hardtops||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-07-2001||03:28 PM||||I wanted to get feedback from owners of Fiero's with T tops. I have been thinking about getting one in the future. I know they look very nice but are they worth it? Are there a lot of leakage problems, wind noise, less security? Also a concern is the lack of replacement parts and their cost. How well do the seals and associated parts hold up? Also I would not be installing a kit, just a different vehicle.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||01-07-2001||03:40 PM||||I had T-tops on my '86 Trans Am and I'll never buy another car with them again. The car was basically junk so the tops leaked and started rusting out the body. But that wasn't the reason. When I had them out they worked precisely like a parachute. Every time the wind blew, you could feel the car slow down. I don't know if a Fiero will do that since it doesn't have as much room to fill up with air, but personally, I'd rather have a sunroof.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||01-07-2001||04:44 PM||||The worst thing I have found with t-tops is that the parts are so expensive, especially with NO competition in the market.  I got lucky and found an extra set of t-tops for a reasonable price.  I bought them so I wouldn't be SOL if something happened to mine, then I would have to pay a ridiculous amount for another t-top.<P>I had more wind noise in my sunroof Fiero then in my t-top Fiero.  The passenger side does rattle so I have to get that straightened out.  Have to give props to Mike for fixing my drivers side, now its tight and doesn't rattle one bit.<P>I like t-tops, but I wouldn't pay too much extra for a Fiero with them, maybe if its an original 88 but if it was a pre-88 t-top I wouldn't pay more for somewhat equal cars with t-tops/sunroof being the difference....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||01-07-2001||04:55 PM||||I have learned that over time almost all GM tops leak.  My 77 Cutlass, 89 TA and my 88 Fiero all leak.  I keep it in the garage during rain and nothing beats cruise night with the Tops off.  Sometimes its worth it.<P><P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||01-07-2001||06:40 PM||||I've got an '88 coupe with the factory option installed. Never have any problems with leaks, just the 'p' seals dry rotted.<BR>Excellent to drive with them out, totally different than a sunroof! Not had any problems with security.||||reg||1
